{"analytic_contract": {"contract_id": "warrantroute-bounded-source-warrant", "contract_version": "qwen3-generalist-private-pilot-v1", "task_description": "Assess whether displayed excerpts warrant the proposed bounded interpretation.", "validity_rules": ["Every material claim must be warranted by displayed evidence.", "Consequential differences, counterevidence, and boundary cases must remain visible.", "Claim breadth and strength must match displayed source coverage.", "Do not infer diagnoses, identities, prevalence, or causality beyond the packet."]}, "context_note": "Private local diagnostic packet with project-pseudonymous identifiers.", "corpus_id": "dreaddit_test", "evidence": [{"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 1, "excerpt_id": "EXC_cbc344db5a86fdc1", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_a2815787e8bc6094", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Recently a family member of mine called the police on their boyfriend bc he strangled her and beat her. His charges are strangulation and M2 simple assault. She, for now, doesn't want to press charges which is extremely frustrating. She could possibly save a life by doing so. This man has single handedly ruined her life and has been in trouble with the law time and time again."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_d3436a690d74e1c1", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_2dc3f7bd270a546c", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "She's the first person I've ever really opened up to. I haven't told her everything about whats happened, but she does know about my anxiety (which I get from my PTSD) and she reacts sportively to it. To some extent, I let me be \"myself\" around her, whatever I am. She's moving. She's moving to Maryland.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 2, "excerpt_id": "EXC_d3436a690d74e1c1", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_2dc3f7bd270a546c", "speaker_id": null, "text": "She's the first person I've ever really opened up to. I haven't told her everything about whats happened, but she does know about my anxiety (which I get from my PTSD) and she reacts sportively to it. To some extent, I let me be \"myself\" around her, whatever I am. She's moving. She's moving to Maryland."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_cd405367a5f230cd", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_0fbbda30737d8843", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "After getting startled, I have this thing where I'm really angry and defensive for 30-120 minutes afterwards. I can put myself in the most calm of situations, but the duration of this seems to be somewhat independent of my environment. I'm guessing this is because my PTSD brain does not respond well to stress hormones? Sometimes I try to push through it and just go about my day anyway, but it's usually counter-productive. I'd like to train my service dog to alert to the physiological change.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 3, "excerpt_id": "EXC_cd405367a5f230cd", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_0fbbda30737d8843", "speaker_id": null, "text": "After getting startled, I have this thing where I'm really angry and defensive for 30-120 minutes afterwards. I can put myself in the most calm of situations, but the duration of this seems to be somewhat independent of my environment. I'm guessing this is because my PTSD brain does not respond well to stress hormones? Sometimes I try to push through it and just go about my day anyway, but it's usually counter-productive. I'd like to train my service dog to alert to the physiological change."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_790ce08762f57e9b", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_4597e1bfb9a0a044", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "While presenting today, I had absoluly no flight-or-flight panic even when in an confrontational, adversarial discussion about sports or politics. I've always gotten a little flustered during these types of conversations in the past. I'm even witty at times. Please do give this supplement a try. Best of luck.", "candidate_role": "counterevidence", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as a boundary case or counterexample.", "display_order": 4, "excerpt_id": "EXC_790ce08762f57e9b", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_4597e1bfb9a0a044", "speaker_id": null, "text": "While presenting today, I had absoluly no flight-or-flight panic even when in an confrontational, adversarial discussion about sports or politics. I've always gotten a little flustered during these types of conversations in the past. I'm even witty at times. Please do give this supplement a try. Best of luck."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 5, "excerpt_id": "EXC_d2ea6154d09b71c0", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_7c7088b1f2454d7b", "speaker_id": null, "text": "I screamed and my mum helped me until I passed out. I went to the doctor the next day and they referred me on to get a diagnosis for PTSD as well. I get flashies about once every couple of months now and it gets more and more terrifying each time. About a year and a half before GCSE's (finals for you Americans) my anxiety started to show. I would be super stressed about every little test in school and had a baseline amount of stress building up as I got closer to my exam dates."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 6, "excerpt_id": "EXC_2754600db91cd3d9", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_fc4c8ccd31827063", "speaker_id": null, "text": "So I had to look for work again. She gave me hell the entire time. I just found another job at the end of February, but my start date wouldn't be till near the end of march. That wasn't good enough for her (as if I set the start date), so she breaks up with me, and kicks me out. Now I'm fucked, because I have work."}], "item_id": "DJI_96cbf8e665e8c530", "item_schema_version": "direction-j-evaluator-item-v1", "output_id": "OUT_96cbf8e665e8c530", "packet_id": "PKT_9ff5de62ccc9e334", "proposed_interpretation": {"boundary_conditions": ["The context is a discussion about personal experiences with stress and anxiety.", "The participants are individuals who have experienced trauma or stress in their lives."], "claim": "Stress can be triggered by various factors, including past traumas, current situations, and social interactions.", "explanation": "The excerpts suggest that stress can be caused by a range of factors. For example, EXC_d3436a690d74e1c1 describes how the speaker's anxiety is triggered by their PTSD, while EXC_cd405367a5f230cd mentions how the speaker gets angry and defensive after being startled. Additionally, EXC_2754600db91cd3d9 describes a situation where the speaker was stressed due to a breakup and job loss.", "theme_id": "THM_96cbf8e665e8c530", "theme_name": "Stress triggers"}, "research_question": "How do people describe and contextualize experiences of stress?", "source_coverage": {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 3, "candidate_cited_source_count": 3, "coverage_note": "Counts describe only this restricted private packet.", "presented_excerpt_count": 6, "presented_source_count": 6, "sampling_frame_excerpt_count": 6, "sampling_frame_source_count": 6, "source_distribution": [{"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_0fbbda30737d8843"}, {"candidate_cited_ex